.Sh DESCRIPTION
A session manages one or more BitTorrent downloads and seeds.
It owns the event loop integration, listening socket, DHT node, and LSD
announcer.
Torrents added to a session share these resources.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_session_new
creates a session with explicit configuration.
The
.Fa cfg
structure controls storage backend, piece picker, listen port,
timeouts, and optional HTTP tracker callback.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_session_default
creates a session with sensible defaults: file storage at
.Fa path ,
rarest-first picker, listen on port 6881.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_session_free
destroys the session and all its torrents.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_session_run
enters the event loop.
Returns when
.Fn mbt_session_stop
is called or an error occurs.
Callers that run their own event loop do not need to call this.
.Ss Adding torrents
.Fn mbt_session_add_torrent_file
loads a
.Pa .torrent
file from disk.
.Fn mbt_session_add_torrent_buf
parses bencoded metainfo from a buffer.
.Fn mbt_session_add_magnet
adds a torrent by magnet URI; metadata is fetched from peers
via BEP 9.
.Fn mbt_session_add_infohash
adds a bare infohash with no metadata or trackers (useful with DHT).
.Pp
All add functions return 0 on success or a negative errno on failure.
.Ss Torrent enumeration
.Fn mbt_session_torrent_count
returns the number of active torrents.
.Fn mbt_session_torrent_first
and
.Fn mbt_session_torrent_next
iterate them.
.Fn mbt_session_find_torrent
looks up a torrent by infohash.
.Fn mbt_session_remove_torrent
removes and frees a torrent.
.Ss Peer discovery
.Fn mbt_session_enable_dht
starts the DHT node (BEP 5) on the session's listen port.
.Fn mbt_session_dht_bootstrap
adds a known node for initial routing table population.
.Fn mbt_session_dht_get_peers
initiates a DHT lookup for a specific infohash.
.Fn mbt_session_enable_lsd
enables Local Service Discovery (BEP 14) multicast announcements.
.Fn mbt_session_add_peer
manually adds a peer address for a torrent.
.Ss Tracker interaction
.Fn mbt_session_reannounce
forces a re-announce to all trackers.
If
.Fa ih
is non-NULL, only the matching torrent is re-announced.
.Ss Callbacks
.Fn mbt_session_set_callbacks
registers optional session-level event handlers:
.Bl -tag -width on_torrent_complete
.It Fn on_torrent_complete
All pieces verified.
.It Fn on_torrent_error
Fatal error on a torrent.
.It Fn on_lsd_announce
LSD discovery of a peer.
Return 1 to auto-add, 0 to ignore.
.El
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Functions returning
.Ft int
return 0 on success or a negative errno value on failure.
Functions returning a pointer return NULL on failure.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal
struct mbt_session *s;
mbt_session_default(&s, "/tmp/downloads");
mbt_session_enable_dht(s);
mbt_session_dht_bootstrap(s, "router.bittorrent.com", 6881);
mbt_session_add_magnet(s, "magnet:?xt=urn:btih:...");
mbt_session_run(s);
mbt_session_free(s);
.Ed
